---
import MiniMonitor from './illustrations/MiniMonitor.astro';
import Cursor from './illustrations/Cursor.astro';
---

<section id="features" class="section" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="sec-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Features</p>
      <h2 id="features-title">Drawn zones that remember their windows. <span class="soft">The memory part is Windows-only today.</span></h2>
    </header>

    <ul class="grid">
      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="pair">
            <MiniMonitor layout="priority" />
            <MiniMonitor layout="grid" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>A layout for every monitor</h3>
        <p>Each monitor keeps its own layouts. Unplug one, plug it back in, and its layouts return.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="tpls">
            <div class="ill-ed__thumb"><i style="--x:4%;--w:45%" /><i style="--x:51%;--w:45%" /></div>
            <div class="ill-ed__thumb"><i style="--x:4%;--w:29%" /><i style="--x:35.5%;--w:29%" /><i style="--x:67%;--w:29%" /></div>
            <div class="ill-ed__thumb">
              <i style="--x:4%;--y:8%;--w:44%;--h:40%" /><i style="--x:52%;--y:8%;--w:44%;--h:40%" />
              <i style="--x:4%;--y:52%;--w:44%;--h:40%" /><i style="--x:52%;--y:52%;--w:44%;--h:40%" />
            </div>
            <div class="ill-ed__thumb"><i style="--x:4%;--w:21%" /><i style="--x:27%;--w:46%" /><i style="--x:75%;--w:21%" /></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>A visual zone editor, and layout files</h3>
        <p>Start from halves, thirds, a 2x2 grid or priority, or split and drag the dividers until it fits. Undo and save as you go. Copy a layout as plain text to keep it or to add it on another monitor or computer: zones are proportions, so one text fits any screen.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="pair">
            <MiniMonitor layout="grid" off label="Unplugged" />
            <MiniMonitor layout="grid" label="Plugged back in" win={[0, 3]} />
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Zones that remember their windows <span class="tag">Windows</span></h3>
        <p>When a monitor comes back, the windows you snapped to it go back into their zones. It lives in memory only, with no window titles, and a window you move yourself is left alone. Tested with a simulated monitor change, not yet a real unplug.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="keyrows">
            <p><kbd class="on">Ctrl</kbd><kbd class="on">Alt</kbd><kbd class="on">Shift</kbd></p>
            <p><kbd>&larr;</kbd><kbd>&rarr;</kbd><kbd>1&ndash;9</kbd><kbd>&uarr;</kbd></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Move windows from the keyboard <span class="tag">Windows</span></h3>
        <p>Ctrl+Alt+Shift with Left or Right steps through the zones, 1 to 9 jumps to one, Up sends the window to the next monitor. Pick other modifier keys if something else already uses these; Settings lists any it could not register.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="linked" viewBox="0 0 220 90" focusable="false">
            <rect class="win" x="6" y="6" width="104" height="66" rx="7"></rect>
            <rect class="win" x="118" y="6" width="96" height="66" rx="7"></rect>
            <path class="old" d="M148 2v74"></path>
            <path class="trail" d="M146 83H124"></path>
            <path class="trail" d="M130 78l-6 5 6 5"></path>
          </svg>
          <div class="art-label"><span>drag an edge</span><span>neighbours follow</span></div>
        </div>
        <h3>Linked dividers <span class="tag tag--warn">Windows, early</span></h3>
        <p>Resize a snapped window by its edge and the snapped windows that share that edge follow when you let go. Early: it works in tests with synthetic events, but a real mouse drag has not been confirmed yet.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="keys">
            <kbd class="on">Shift</kbd><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>Alt</kbd><kbd>Win</kbd>
          </div>
          <div class="art-label"><span>120 ms or instant</span><span>gap 0&ndash;32 px</span></div>
        </div>
        <h3>Your key, your pace, your gap</h3>
        <p>Hold Shift by default, or Ctrl, Alt or the Windows key (Command on a Mac), to show the zones. Moves glide in about 120 ms or jump at once. Leave 0 to 32 px between zones if you like air around your windows.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="pair">
            <MiniMonitor layout="thirds" label="100%" />
            <MiniMonitor layout="thirds" label="150%" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Careful with windows</h3>
        <p>On Windows, Krova accounts for mixed-DPI monitors (not yet verified on a mixed setup), the invisible borders around windows, each app&rsquo;s own minimum and maximum size, and the taskbar.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card">
        <div class="art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="edge ill-wrap">
            <div class="ill-monitor ill-monitor--mini">
              <div class="ill-desk">
                <div class="ill-work">
                  <span class="ill-zone ill-zone--solid" style="--x:0.8%;--w:48.6%" />
                  <span class="ill-zone ill-zone--soft" style="--x:50.6%;--w:48.6%" />
                  <Cursor x="1%" y="38%" />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Edge snapping, if you want it</h3>
        <p>Drag to a side for a half, a corner for a quarter, the top to maximize. Off by default, and never on the border between two monitors.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="also">
      Also: a tray icon with launch at login. Light and dark follow your system. Minimized, fullscreen and administrator
      windows are skipped. Closing Krova&rsquo;s window closes the embedded browser too, so it waits in the tray using little memory.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }

  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: var(--space-s);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
  }

  .art {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    min-height: 11rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-m);
    padding: var(--space-m);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
  }

  .card h3 {
    padding-inline: var(--space-xs);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }

  .card p {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xs);
    padding: 0 var(--space-xs) var(--space-xs);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 18rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .tpls {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 14rem;
  }
  .tpls .ill-ed__thumb {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .edge {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 12rem;
  }

  .linked {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 15rem;
    height: auto;
  }
  .linked .win {
    fill: var(--ill-hi-fill);
    stroke: var(--ill-hi-stroke);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .linked .old {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--ill-line-strong);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
  }
  .linked .trail {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-text-soft);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
  .art-label {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 15rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  .keys {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .keys kbd {
    min-width: 3rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .keys kbd.on,
  .keyrows kbd.on {
    border-color: var(--ill-key-on-edge);
    background: var(--ill-key-on-bg);
    color: var(--ill-key-on-text);
  }

  .keyrows {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    justify-items: center;
  }
  .keyrows p {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .keyrows kbd {
    min-width: 2.75rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .keyrows kbd.on {
    color: var(--ill-key-on-text);
  }

  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.08rem 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    vertical-align: 0.15em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .tag--warn {
    background: var(--color-warn-bg);
    border-color: var(--color-warn-border);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .also {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: var(--space-l) auto 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  /* Three columns, written as six so the last two of the eight cards share the final row (span 3 each). */
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
    .grid > .card {
      grid-column: span 2;
    }
    .grid > .card:nth-child(n + 7) {
      grid-column: span 3;
    }
  }
</style>
